{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161823-fresh-pack-what-to-do-with-them","id":161823,"title":"Fresh pack - what to do with them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-07T10:06:46-07:00","id":161823,"title":"Fresh pack - what to do with them?","content":"So my pack of Wolf-Blooded become pack of young Uratha after successful hunt for they Totem and intervention of Winter Wolf. They still will try to convince the indivdual Firstborns for they protection as Tribe Totems, but as the pack they look as all settled. They have Bale Hounds enemies nerby, but for now they lay low and want to become true Uratha to oppose more experienced Hounds when they are prepared,<br /> <br /> So my question is simple - <b>what can fresh werewolves pack do?</b><br /> <br /> I was thinking they could look for or creat Locus so they could start to crave they own territory. They Totem is weak now - only awoken by them from years of spiritual hibernation - and he is placed in Shadow Realm Barren. And they have they Bale Hounds enemies, What would you advise on starting to do now in chronicle?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T10:19:19-07:00","id":161850,"title":"","content":"Adjust to life as a Forsaken - you're not human anymore. Focus on the human side of things, and demonstrate to the players how their characters will find it difficult to lead normal, sane human lives from now on. Relationships go wrong because of the rage, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Also, for general story hooks, I recommend checking out my story hooks thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T10:56:57-07:00","id":161865,"title":"","content":"Carving out a locus and territory is a good start - maybe a nice, physical threat for them to handle. Some form of changing breed who dislike shaving uratha horning in on their turf? The wolf must hunt, so give them some prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:25:16-07:00","id":161917,"title":"","content":"Throw them into something immediately dangerous and werewolf, like having to defeat a ridden cult or claimed that's tearing apart local loci that once helped feed the totem.<br /> <br /> Nothing bonds people like committing a crime (except for who it doesn't), plus then when they get some 'down time' they can worry about the consequences of their actions as well as go over how they dealt with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-07-2014, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T15:01:13-07:00","id":161988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161823-fresh-pack-what-to-do-with-them?p=161865#post161865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carving out a locus and territory is a good start - maybe a nice, physical threat for them to handle. Some form of changing breed who dislike shaving uratha horning in on their turf? The wolf must hunt, so give them some prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about putting Ursara ( from <b>Changing Breeds</b> ) before, as this is Scandinavia. Gay Ursara, to be precise. Because, you know, <a href=\"http://www.tmediapromotion.com/awerebearstale/images/werebear2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>gay (were)bear</b></a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( It was mentioned to me I didn't put any obvious LGBT character lately, so I will make one I could accord with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> But to be serious, I was thinking he is last of long line of Ursara that tender the bear now Totem spirit of the Pack, but he forsake his duties for life of hedonism/seclusion/any-other-shifters-temptation. He abandon sacred duty and now Totem is weak because of him. Could be very interesting character if you think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161823-fresh-pack-what-to-do-with-them?p=161917#post161917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throw them into something immediately dangerous and werewolf, like having to defeat a ridden cult or claimed that's tearing apart local loci that once helped feed the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have ridden cult - in the town few kilometers away were the cult is run by Bale Hounds they lay low from... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So I will abstain from this, especially, as I want some &quot;calm&quot; session for now. But idea is good to return when characters will be more stable in the pack roles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:53:03-07:00","id":163920,"title":"","content":"Here's a fun one. They find out the local church they used to attend is run by a Bale Hound of pride. They wouldn't have noticed it previously, but now that they've shifted that can see the world 'clearly' for the first time. Including the beast in their midst. <br /> <br /> Let's not forget that bale hounds in europe out number the Pure and Forsaken by a large margin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T11:47:05-07:00","id":164978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161823-fresh-pack-what-to-do-with-them?p=163920#post163920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a fun one. They find out the local church they used to attend is run by a Bale Hound of pride. They wouldn't have noticed it previously, but now that they've shifted that can see the world 'clearly' for the first time. Including the beast in their midst.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was my idea from all along, only with Hound of Envy. From write-up of Bale Hounds in <b>Blasphemies</b> I got vibe that Pride Hounds want people to woriship him as him - i.e. 2,5 meters high beast of rage, not priest in church. He wants too boos his PRIDE, don't he? I assumed that Envy would take over church congregation as point of xenophobia, intolerance and even to build up in community spirit &quot;your neighbor must be worse in eyes of God than you&quot;. Like this little community...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/ehjWWgdrY_Q\" data-code=\"ehjWWgdrY_Q\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ehjWWgdrY_Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And this stuff I prepered for later part of chronicle, when players will be at least full aware Uratha. Destroying Bale Hounds was the goal the pack was created in first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161823-fresh-pack-what-to-do-with-them?p=163920#post163920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget that bale hounds in europe out number the Pure and Forsaken by a large margin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting - were is more on this subject? Maybe I can get even more info on Bale Hounds... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-10-2014, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T16:09:59-07:00","id":166313,"title":"","content":"It's in shadows of the uk. The spirits there make use of all the Christian lore that werewolves must be evil so they whisper dread things to them, and when they change they assume they're evil so why not? It's one of the only places with full bale hound packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T18:35:36-07:00","id":166423,"title":"","content":"Interesting to be looking for stuff to Northern Sweded in UK book... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But this idea was mine also - Christianity run Spirits in to 7 Deadly Sins ( or 7 Celestial Virtue ), so many Uratha become Bale Hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T07:40:44-07:00","id":166925,"title":"","content":"It actually makes a whole lotta sense. Sucks for the hounds when they realize how wrong they are... Dunno how much it matters though. From what I understand post ww2 European hisil is a royal mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}